# RSpade release tree: byte-fidelity is REQUIRED.
#
# A downstream checkout must materialize EXACTLY the bytes the monorepo committed.
# If git normalized line endings, a checkout would materialize LF where an upstream
# package (e.g. vendored node_modules shipping CRLF) stored CRLF - and every such
# file would then read as modified on every pull, churn that is not a change.
# Disable all text/eol conversion so the committed blobs and every checkout are
# byte-for-byte identical to the tree published here.
#
# git honors .gitattributes per-directory, so this file also governs the vendored
# rspade_project copy of this tree (system/**) and every converted downstream app
# repo automatically - no separate file is needed there.
* -text
